==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|cheap|-en<id:inchoative>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtʃiːpən/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-cheapen.oga|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[decrease]] the [[value]] or [[price]] of; to make [[cheap]]er.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[vulgar]].
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=13 August 2017|author=Brandon Nowalk|title=Oldtown Offers One Last Game-changing Secret as {{w|Game of Thrones}} Goes behind Enemy Lines (Newbies)|work=[[w:The A.V. Club|The Onion A.V. Club]]|url=http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/oldtown-offers-one-last-game-changing-secret-game--259407|passage=The pace of the season can't help but '''cheapen''' these scenes, but I can’t deny that it's a blast. I’ve been critical of both the relative depopulation of the cast in this final run and the speedy, schematic narrative that checks off high points and moves on without really building to them.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170817060914/http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/oldtown-offers-one-last-game-changing-secret-game--259407|archivedate=17 August 2017|accessdate=17 August 2017}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become cheaper.
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To bargain for, ask the price of.
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Four Georges|pages=34–35|pageref=34|passage=I should like to have seen that noble old madcap Peterborough in his boots (he actually had the audacity to walk about Bath in boots!), with his blue ribbon and stars, and a cabbage under each arm, and a chicken in his hand, which he had been '''cheapening''' for his dinner.}}
#* {{RQ:Le Fanu House|passage=The maid was on the step, '''cheapening''' fish with a virulent lady who had a sieve-full to dispose of.}}

